---
title: Journal
layout: home
description: Short, dated, unpolished. The things that are too small to be posts and too useful to lose — a working log, not a blog.
eyebrow: Collections
source: src/components/timeline.css · collection.css
---
<section class="im-section im-wrap" style="padding-top: 1.5rem; --im-section-gap: 1.5rem">
	<p class="im-eyebrow">Collections · {{page.title}}</p>
	<p class="im-lede">{{page.description}}</p>
	<p class="doc-source"><code>{{page.source}}</code></p>
</section>

<div class="im-single im-wrap" data-sidebar="on">
	<article class="im-stack" style="--im-stack-gap: 2rem">
		<header class="im-collhead">
			<p class="im-eyebrow">Journal</p>
			<h1 class="im-collhead-title">Working notes</h1>
			<p class="im-collhead-text">Things that are too small to be posts and too useful to lose. Written the day they happened and not tidied up afterwards.</p>
			<p class="im-collhead-meta"><span>{{demo.journal.length}} entries this month</span><span>Since 2023</span><a href="#entries">RSS</a></p>
		</header>

		<ol class="im-timeline im-log" id="entries" style="--im-timeline-gap: 2rem">
			{{#each demo.journal}}
			<li class="im-timeline-item">
				<span class="im-timeline-marker"></span>
				<time class="im-timeline-time">{{when}}</time>
				<h2 class="im-timeline-title">{{title}}</h2>
				<p class="im-timeline-text">{{text}}</p>
				<p class="im-log-meta"><a class="im-tag" href="/collections/tag/page/">{{tag}}</a><span class="im-kind" data-kind="post">{{icon "pencil"}}Note</span></p>
			</li>
			{{/each}}
		</ol>

		<div class="im-loadmore">
			<button class="im-btn" type="button">Earlier entries</button>
			<p>4 of 318</p>
		</div>
	</article>

	<aside>
		<div class="im-sticky-rail">
			<div class="im-widgets">
				<section class="im-widget" aria-labelledby="j-now">
					<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="j-now">Now <a href="#entries">Sep 2026</a></h2>
					<ul class="im-widget-now">
						<li>{{icon "code"}}<span>Building <b>collections</b></span></li>
						<li>{{icon "book-open"}}<span>Reading <b>The Peregrine</b></span></li>
						<li>{{icon "map-pin"}}<span>In <b>Budapest</b></span></li>
					</ul>
				</section>

				<section class="im-widget" aria-labelledby="j-archive">
					<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="j-archive">By month</h2>
					<nav class="im-widget-archive" aria-label="Journal archive">
						<a href="#entries" style="--im-share: 100%">September<small>12</small></a>
						<a href="#entries" style="--im-share: 74%">August<small>9</small></a>
						<a href="#entries" style="--im-share: 58%">July<small>7</small></a>
						<a href="#entries" style="--im-share: 33%">June<small>4</small></a>
					</nav>
				</section>

				<section class="im-widget im-widget-fill" aria-labelledby="j-sub">
					<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="j-sub">Follow along</h2>
					<p class="im-widget-heading">Notes by email, monthly.</p>
					{{> "components/subscribe" id="journal-email" button="Join"}}
				</section>
			</div>
		</div>
	</aside>
</div>

<section class="im-section im-wrap">
	<div class="im-prose">
		<h2>A journal is a timeline, not a feed</h2>
		<p>The difference matters. A feed of cards says "each of these is a thing worth clicking"; a journal says "here is everything, in order, read as much as you like". So it is the <a href="/components/timeline/">timeline</a> — dated marks down a line, the entry beside each one, and no card, no picture and no read-more.</p>
		<p>There is no individual page. An entry <strong>is</strong> its content, and a page containing four sentences and a footer is a worse way to read four sentences.</p>
		<div class="im-table-scroll">
		<table>
			<thead><tr><th>Choice</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td>Timeline, not cards</td><td>Entries are read in sequence, not chosen between.</td></tr>
				<tr><td>No excerpt, no clamp</td><td>If it is too long to print whole, it is a <a href="/collections/post/">post</a>.</td></tr>
				<tr><td>Date first, title second</td><td>A journal is navigated by when, not by what.</td></tr>
				<tr><td>An archive by month, not by year</td><td>Because there are three hundred of them.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		</div>

		<h2>In a theme</h2>
		{{{{code "hbs"}}}}
{{#get "posts" filter="tag:#note" limit="20"}}
	<ol class="im-timeline im-log">
		{{#foreach posts}}
		<li class="im-timeline-item">
			<span class="im-timeline-marker"></span>
			<time class="im-timeline-time">{{date format="D MMMM"}}</time>
			<h2 class="im-timeline-title">{{title}}</h2>
			<div class="im-timeline-text">{{content}}</div>
		</li>
		{{/foreach}}
	</ol>
{{/get}}
		{{{{/code}}}}
		<p><code>{{"{{content}}"}}</code>, not <code>{{"{{excerpt}}"}}</code> — the whole entry, on the list page. That is the format.</p>
	</div>
</section>
